cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this research project, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "VeriFace AI: a research study of face-image authenticity classification, robustness and its limits"
authors:
  - given-names: Anshu
    family-names: Raj
repository-code: "https://github.com/Anshu-raj-co/VeriFace-AI"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-16"
keywords:
  - deepfake detection
  - face forensics
  - EfficientNet
  - Grad-CAM
  - generalisation
  - calibration
abstract: >-
  An EfficientNet-B0 classifier for genuine vs AI-generated / manipulated face
  images, trained on 164,760 audited, group-split face crops. The project
  documents leave-family-out generalisation (not supported for unseen
  generator families), JPEG robustness, calibration, a validation-derived
  three-way verdict policy and Grad-CAM explainability. It is a research
  prototype, not a forensic tool.
